## Session 35 — final summary

**Criteria NOT met** (dir_reuse_coherency 8/tcp still ~4/5), but this session achieved the decisive **root-cause proof** that ~130 prior sessions missed.

**Proven root** (via `dirwr=1` write-trace + two GPT-5.5 consults on the captured data): the round-1 dir_reuse loss is a **block→leaf format-transition coherency bug**. `xfs_dir2_block_to_leaf` reuses dir block 0's daddr (block-format → data-format, in-place) **without advancing the cluster-visible dir generation**. So pre-conversion buffers stay `bgen == dirgen == 2` — "current" to every gen/epoch/incarnation guard — and a later AIL/delwri writeback of that stale block-format image overwrites the post-add data block, durably dropping a dirent. Captured byte-exact: node7 journals `node7_f1`→daddr120, then daddr120 is written (by node7 itself, then node6 as `xfs_dir3_block`) without it, all gen=2.

**This explains why every prior fix failed** — they're all blind to a divergence the generation counter doesn't track.

**Refuted this session** (all blind to the conversion-gen root; all over-fire/wedge): epoch-never-0 (readdir=0), addname_epoch_refresh (readdir=0), subset_guard (wedge), reflush_skip (readdir=0/2), dir_release_stale (buffer re-enters).

**Fix direction for next session** (GPT-5.5 confirmed, recorded in `sess35-FIX-DIRECTION-gen-bump-on-conversion-and-per-handoff`):
1. Bump `i_dlm_dir_gen` + stamp the live buffer **in** `xfs_dir2_block_to_leaf` (and sf_to_block/leaf_to_node), same transaction — handoff-independent, makes pre-conversion buffers detectably stale (`bgen < dirgen`) so the existing write-submit gen-guard suppresses only them (reliable → no wedge).
2. Investigate why the existing `mxfs_dir_gen_per_handoff=1` lever (whose comment describes this exact bug) isn't advancing `dirgen` per handoff in round-1 (the `<= loaded_gen` cap / fast-path handoff gap).

**State left clean:** keeper build `4703FA18` (≡ 2EAA0090, 4/5) on disk, source reverted to baseline (epoch-never-0 removed), all experimental params default-off, no leftover processes, decisive trace saved at `tests/tcp/drc_cap/SESS35_daddr120_trace.txt`. I have not written the criteria marker — work continues in the next session from this proven diagnosis.

